### 03 - Create Multiple GCP VMs Using gcloud

#### Create 3 VMs at Once

```bash
gcloud compute instances create vm-1 vm-2 vm-3 \
  --zone=us-central1-a \
  --machine-type=e2-micro
```

#### Verify VMs

```bash
gcloud compute instances list
```

#### Delete 3 VMs at Once

```bash
gcloud compute instances delete vm-1 vm-2 vm-3 \
  --zone=us-central1-a
```

#### Delete Without Confirmation

```bash
gcloud compute instances delete vm-1 vm-2 vm-3 \
  --zone=us-central1-a \
  --quiet
```

#### Verify After Deletion

```bash
gcloud compute instances list
```
What We Learned

Managing a small number of VMs using gcloud commands is manageable.

But when the infrastructure grows, manually managing the number of commands becomes a challenge.

For example:

3 VMs → manageable
10 VMs → more commands
50 VMs → difficult to manage
100+ VMs → manual command management becomes challenging
Multiple environments/projects → even more difficult

We need a better way to create, manage, modify, and reproduce infrastructure using code.

👉 This is where Terraform comes into the picture.

